{{!--
    reference/token-alert - "no access token set" banner shown at the top of the reference
    pages. Server-rendered but hidden by default; static/js/reference.js unhides it when
    the tab holds no token, because whether one is set is client state.

    The banner sticks below the topbar instead of scrolling away, because the Try it panels
    it warns about sit hundreds of pixels down a group page - a warning only visible at the
    top of the page is read once and then gone. Sticky, not fixed: the band keeps its place
    in normal flow, so at rest it pushes the page down instead of covering it, and it takes
    the page background with it so operations passing underneath do not show through.
    Nothing ends up permanently hidden behind it either - reference.js publishes the band's
    measured height as --ee-sticky-band-h, and the layout's scroll-padding (.ee-app-chrome in
    app.tailwind.css) adds it to the scroller's top inset, so anything scrolled into view -
    a deep link, find-in-page, the focus moving through a Try it panel - lands below it.

    Rendered only when a token is actually required: with the `disableTokens` setting on,
    the API accepts uncredentialed callers, so the banner would be wrong.

    Not shown on the access-token page itself - the control is already there.
--}}
{{#unless disableTokens}}
{{!-- -mx-6/px-6 is the content column's own gutter (views/layout/app.hbs), cancelled out so
      the opaque band reaches the column edges and nothing scrolls up beside it. The vertical
      padding is the rest of that band: it keeps a strip of page background between the alert
      and whatever is passing underneath, instead of content touching the alert's edge. Both
      pairs cancel to the spacing this banner had before it became sticky. --}}
<div id="ref-token-alert" class="bg-base-200 @container sticky top-topbar z-20 -mx-6 -mt-2 mb-3 hidden px-6 pt-2 pb-3">
    {{!-- One row wherever there is room for one: with wrapping on, flex breaks the line on the
          text's full width, so the actions drop below it even where they would have fitted
          beside a text column half as wide. Asked of the container rather than the viewport,
          because the constraint is this column - at lg the sidebar and the section nav take
          544px out of the window, and a viewport breakpoint would unwrap the band exactly
          where the column is at its narrowest, stacking the sentence seven lines high. 42rem
          is where the text still fits two lines beside the actions: measured 84-94px for the
          one-row form above it, against 168px for the wrapped form below it. --}}
    <div class="alert alert-soft alert-warning flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 @2xl:flex-nowrap" role="alert">
        <span class="icon-[tabler--key-off] size-5 shrink-0"></span>
        <div class="min-w-0 grow text-sm">
            No access token is set, so <strong>Try it</strong> requests will be rejected with a 401.
        </div>
        <div class="flex shrink-0 flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            {{> ui/btn variant="primary" size="sm" icon="icon-[tabler--clock-plus]" label="Mint temporary token"
            class="ref-token-mint" id="" href="" style="" bare="" type="" overlay="" external=""}}
            {{> ui/btn href="/admin/reference/token" variant="neutral" style="soft" size="sm" label="Set a token"
            icon="" id="" bare="" type="" overlay="" external=""}}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{{/unless}}
